I left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`, and `wasm32-unknown-unknown` without a WASI adapter has no network access. An HTTP call would need an `http-client` import. That would add authority the graph doesn't grant, and the build would reject it. It would also send the untrusted message text to an outside host. If you need enrichment, it has to be added in the graph as a capability for this node or as a separate node. The node's output is unchanged.

The build failed because `Intent` isn't named in the world's `use`, so wit-bindgen puts it in `crate::aap::caps::types` rather than at the crate root. I added the import for it.

